diff --git a/PR.md b/PR.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0cb70ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PR.md
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+# Audit remediation: ownership, report path, cent-exact money, dead code
+
+Audit of `orders-service` against `README.md` ("Rules" is the authoritative
+statement of intent) plus a structural pass over `src/`. Six defects and four
+simplifications; no new dependency, no behavior added beyond what the README
+already promises.
+
+## What changed
+
+### Security
+
+| | Defect | Fix |
+|:--|:--|:--|
+| 1 | `GET /orders/:id` returned any order to any authenticated customer: the handler called the unguarded `orders.get(id)` instead of the ownership-checked `orders.getOwned(user, id)`. README: "Customers read and change only their own orders". | `src/orders/routes.js` passes the caller; `src/orders/service.js` no longer exports `get` at all, so an unguarded single-order read is not reachable from any route. The remaining `get` callers are the admin-gated lifecycle operations inside the service. |
+| 2 | `GET /reports/:name` joined the caller's name onto `REPORT_DIR` after `decodeURIComponent`, so `..%2F…` read any file the process could read. | `src/reports/routes.js` accepts only names of the shape it mints (`/^orders-\d+-[0-9a-f]{6}\.csv$/`) and returns 404 otherwise; the name never reaches `path.join` unless it matches. One regex is both the mint and the accept rule. |
+| 3 | `tokens.verify` compared the HMAC with `!==`, which short-circuits on the first differing byte. | `src/auth/tokens.js` compares with `crypto.timingSafeEqual` after a length check. |
+
+### Correctness
+
+| | Defect | Fix |
+|:--|:--|:--|
+| 4 | Order totals were summed in binary floating point: `0.1 × 3 + 19.99 × 3` stored `60.269999999999996`, contradicting README "An order total is exact to the cent". The payment check was cent-exact, so such an order could never be paid at its own stated total. | `src/lib/money.js` owns the currency rule and works in integer cents (`toCents`, `totalCents`, `fromCents`). Orders and payments both use it; `payments/service.js` lost its private copy of the cent math. |
+| 5 | `paginate` computed `totalPages` with `Math.floor`, so 25 items at 20 per page reported 1 page and the second page was unreachable by a client that trusts the field. README: "the number of pages needed to show every item, at least 1". | `Math.ceil` in `src/lib/pagination.js`. |
+| 6 | The state table allowed `shipped → cancelled`, contradicting README "a shipped or delivered order can no longer be cancelled". | `shipped: ['delivered']` in `src/orders/service.js`. `paid → cancelled` stays allowed, as the README requires. |
+
+### Dead code and simplification
+
+- **`parseCookies` deleted** (`src/http/respond.js`): zero callers, and the service authenticates only with `Authorization: Bearer`.
+- **Payment provider registry collapsed** (`src/payments/providers.js`): a module-level mutable `Map`, `registerProvider`, `getProvider` and a provider-name string existed for exactly one provider that no caller ever selected. `createPaymentService` now takes the gateway object directly, defaulting to `manualProvider`; the injection seam a second gateway would need is preserved, the registry around it is gone.
+- **Layer skip removed** (`src/users/*`, `src/app.js`): `registerUserRoutes` received the raw `store` and composed `store.list('users').map(users.toPublic)` in the HTTP layer. `GET /users` now calls `users.list(query)`; the service owns its own listing and no longer publishes its row mapper, and no route module receives the store.
